{"seq":1,"at":"2026-09-17","kind":"imported","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0458"},"reason":"Article of the Quiztopia bank (written for card c039): researched and transcribed in September 2026, converted to the quiz platform on 2026-10-20.","by":"Quiztopia import","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/quiztopia/c039.json"},
{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0458"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge literature/classics","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/literature__classics.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",559],["+"," The name has outlived the novel in an unexpected way: in 1969 a London hard-rock band called itself Uriah Heep, so that for many people today it means a 1970s rock group before it means a Dickens villain."],["=",395],["+","was also a performer. From April 1858 he toured Britain and Ireland reading his own work aloud for his own profit – 129 appearances in 49 towns on the first tour alone – which makes him the first great author to give paid public readings. Audiences wept at the death of little Nell and gasped at his Bill Sikes murdering Nancy, and the strain of further tours, including one through America in 1867–1868, wore him out in his last years.\n\nDickens "],["=",69]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",529],["+"," Der Name hat den Roman auf unerwartete Weise überlebt: 1969 nannte sich eine Londoner Hardrock-Band Uriah Heep, sodass er heute für viele zuerst eine Rockgruppe der 1970er-Jahre bezeichnet und erst dann einen Schurken von Dickens."],["=",383],["+","Dickens war auch ein Vortragskünstler. Ab April 1858 reiste er durch Großbritannien und Irland und las auf eigene Rechnung aus seinen Werken – allein auf der ersten Tournee 129 Auftritte in 49 Städten –, womit Charles Dickens als erster großer Autor bezahlte öffentliche Lesungen hielt. Das Publikum weinte beim Tod der kleinen Nell und erschrak, wenn er Bill Sikes den Mord an Nancy begehen ließ, und die Strapazen weiterer Tourneen, darunter eine durch Amerika 1867–1868, zehrten in seinen letzten Jahren an ihm.\n\n"],["=",63]]}]},
